$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Health Communication/Week 08/Practice
::HC-W8-P01::A viral health video has 500,000 views but comments show many viewers interpreted the advice backwards. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=engagement without comprehension#Correct. Exposure metrics do not establish correct interpretation.
~privacy risk in digital messaging#Not the best answer. Exposure metrics do not establish correct interpretation.
~unsafe generative AI deployment#Not the best answer. Exposure metrics do not establish correct interpretation.
~digital exclusion by design#Not the best answer. Exposure metrics do not establish correct interpretation.
}

::HC-W8-P02::A viral health video has 500,000 views but comments show many viewers interpreted the advice backwards. What is the strongest next response? {
=Measure comprehension and correct the ambiguity rather than treating views as success.#Correct. Exposure metrics do not establish correct interpretation.
~Use consented, discreet reminder options and allow users to choose safe channels.#Not the best answer. Exposure metrics do not establish correct interpretation.
~Constrain knowledge sources, define prohibited advice, monitor outputs and escalate high-risk questions to humans.#Not the best answer. Exposure metrics do not establish correct interpretation.
~Offer low-data and offline alternatives such as compressed content, SMS or community channels.#Not the best answer. Exposure metrics do not establish correct interpretation.
}

::HC-W8-P03::An HIV service sends identifiable appointment reminders to shared family phones. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=privacy risk in digital messaging#Correct. Shared-device contexts can reveal sensitive health information.
~unsafe generative AI deployment#Not the best answer. Shared-device contexts can reveal sensitive health information.
~digital exclusion by design#Not the best answer. Shared-device contexts can reveal sensitive health information.
~moderation that suppresses legitimate concern#Not the best answer. Shared-device contexts can reveal sensitive health information.
}

::HC-W8-P04::An HIV service sends identifiable appointment reminders to shared family phones. What is the strongest next response? {
=Use consented, discreet reminder options and allow users to choose safe channels.#Correct. Shared-device contexts can reveal sensitive health information.
~Constrain knowledge sources, define prohibited advice, monitor outputs and escalate high-risk questions to humans.#Not the best answer. Shared-device contexts can reveal sensitive health information.
~Offer low-data and offline alternatives such as compressed content, SMS or community channels.#Not the best answer. Shared-device contexts can reveal sensitive health information.
~Moderate abuse and dangerous misinformation while allowing respectful questions and responding transparently.#Not the best answer. Shared-device contexts can reveal sensitive health information.
}

::HC-W8-P05::A chatbot answers medication questions using a general language model with no clinical knowledge constraints. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=unsafe generative AI deployment#Correct. Fluent output can be wrong or overconfident.
~digital exclusion by design#Not the best answer. Fluent output can be wrong or overconfident.
~moderation that suppresses legitimate concern#Not the best answer. Fluent output can be wrong or overconfident.
~metric-objective mismatch#Not the best answer. Fluent output can be wrong or overconfident.
}

::HC-W8-P06::A chatbot answers medication questions using a general language model with no clinical knowledge constraints. What is the strongest next response? {
=Constrain knowledge sources, define prohibited advice, monitor outputs and escalate high-risk questions to humans.#Correct. Fluent output can be wrong or overconfident.
~Offer low-data and offline alternatives such as compressed content, SMS or community channels.#Not the best answer. Fluent output can be wrong or overconfident.
~Moderate abuse and dangerous misinformation while allowing respectful questions and responding transparently.#Not the best answer. Fluent output can be wrong or overconfident.
~Measure confidence, knowledge of referral options and verified help-seeking in addition to clicks.#Not the best answer. Fluent output can be wrong or overconfident.
}

::HC-W8-P07::A digital campaign is available only through a high-data video app in a low-bandwidth district. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=digital exclusion by design#Correct. Technical availability does not guarantee practical access.
~moderation that suppresses legitimate concern#Not the best answer. Technical availability does not guarantee practical access.
~metric-objective mismatch#Not the best answer. Technical availability does not guarantee practical access.
~algorithmic selection of exposure#Not the best answer. Technical availability does not guarantee practical access.
}

::HC-W8-P08::A digital campaign is available only through a high-data video app in a low-bandwidth district. What is the strongest next response? {
=Offer low-data and offline alternatives such as compressed content, SMS or community channels.#Correct. Technical availability does not guarantee practical access.
~Moderate abuse and dangerous misinformation while allowing respectful questions and responding transparently.#Not the best answer. Technical availability does not guarantee practical access.
~Measure confidence, knowledge of referral options and verified help-seeking in addition to clicks.#Not the best answer. Technical availability does not guarantee practical access.
~Avoid assuming platform reach represents all pregnant women and use complementary recruitment or channels.#Not the best answer. Technical availability does not guarantee practical access.
}
$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Health Communication/Week 08/Mastery
::HC-W8-M01::A social-media page deletes every critical comment about vaccination. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=moderation that suppresses legitimate concern#Correct. Trust can fall when disagreement is treated as misconduct.
~metric-objective mismatch#Not the best answer. Trust can fall when disagreement is treated as misconduct.
~algorithmic selection of exposure#Not the best answer. Trust can fall when disagreement is treated as misconduct.
~group privacy and consent problem#Not the best answer. Trust can fall when disagreement is treated as misconduct.
}

::HC-W8-M02::A social-media page deletes every critical comment about vaccination. What is the strongest next response? {
=Moderate abuse and dangerous misinformation while allowing respectful questions and responding transparently.#Correct. Trust can fall when disagreement is treated as misconduct.
~Measure confidence, knowledge of referral options and verified help-seeking in addition to clicks.#Not the best answer. Trust can fall when disagreement is treated as misconduct.
~Avoid assuming platform reach represents all pregnant women and use complementary recruitment or channels.#Not the best answer. Trust can fall when disagreement is treated as misconduct.
~Explain visibility, obtain informed agreement and offer a private alternative for those who do not want disclosure.#Not the best answer. Trust can fall when disagreement is treated as misconduct.
}

::HC-W8-M03::A programme uses click-through rate as its main indicator for a mental-health campaign whose objective is help-seeking confidence. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=metric-objective mismatch#Correct. Clicks are intermediate platform behaviour, not the intended communication outcome.
~algorithmic selection of exposure#Not the best answer. Clicks are intermediate platform behaviour, not the intended communication outcome.
~group privacy and consent problem#Not the best answer. Clicks are intermediate platform behaviour, not the intended communication outcome.
~potentially deceptive synthetic media#Not the best answer. Clicks are intermediate platform behaviour, not the intended communication outcome.
}

::HC-W8-M04::A programme uses click-through rate as its main indicator for a mental-health campaign whose objective is help-seeking confidence. What is the strongest next response? {
=Measure confidence, knowledge of referral options and verified help-seeking in addition to clicks.#Correct. Clicks are intermediate platform behaviour, not the intended communication outcome.
~Avoid assuming platform reach represents all pregnant women and use complementary recruitment or channels.#Not the best answer. Clicks are intermediate platform behaviour, not the intended communication outcome.
~Explain visibility, obtain informed agreement and offer a private alternative for those who do not want disclosure.#Not the best answer. Clicks are intermediate platform behaviour, not the intended communication outcome.
~Disclose synthetic representation when viewers could reasonably infer a real testimonial or real event.#Not the best answer. Clicks are intermediate platform behaviour, not the intended communication outcome.
}

::HC-W8-M05::An algorithm shows a maternal-health post mostly to users already following health pages. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=algorithmic selection of exposure#Correct. Recommendation systems shape who is exposed.
~group privacy and consent problem#Not the best answer. Recommendation systems shape who is exposed.
~potentially deceptive synthetic media#Not the best answer. Recommendation systems shape who is exposed.
~ambiguous engagement signal#Not the best answer. Recommendation systems shape who is exposed.
}

::HC-W8-M06::An algorithm shows a maternal-health post mostly to users already following health pages. What is the strongest next response? {
=Avoid assuming platform reach represents all pregnant women and use complementary recruitment or channels.#Correct. Recommendation systems shape who is exposed.
~Explain visibility, obtain informed agreement and offer a private alternative for those who do not want disclosure.#Not the best answer. Recommendation systems shape who is exposed.
~Disclose synthetic representation when viewers could reasonably infer a real testimonial or real event.#Not the best answer. Recommendation systems shape who is exposed.
~Review comment content and other evidence before inferring attitudes from reaction counts.#Not the best answer. Recommendation systems shape who is exposed.
}

::HC-W8-M07::A WhatsApp group for chronic-disease patients allows members to see one another’s phone numbers without warning. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=group privacy and consent problem#Correct. Group tools can expose identifiers even when messages are health-related.
~potentially deceptive synthetic media#Not the best answer. Group tools can expose identifiers even when messages are health-related.
~ambiguous engagement signal#Not the best answer. Group tools can expose identifiers even when messages are health-related.
~data minimisation failure#Not the best answer. Group tools can expose identifiers even when messages are health-related.
}

::HC-W8-M08::A WhatsApp group for chronic-disease patients allows members to see one another’s phone numbers without warning. What is the strongest next response? {
=Explain visibility, obtain informed agreement and offer a private alternative for those who do not want disclosure.#Correct. Group tools can expose identifiers even when messages are health-related.
~Disclose synthetic representation when viewers could reasonably infer a real testimonial or real event.#Not the best answer. Group tools can expose identifiers even when messages are health-related.
~Review comment content and other evidence before inferring attitudes from reaction counts.#Not the best answer. Group tools can expose identifiers even when messages are health-related.
~Collect only the data needed for subscription and explain retention and use.#Not the best answer. Group tools can expose identifiers even when messages are health-related.
}

::HC-W8-M09::A health ministry uses an AI-generated image of a fictional patient without disclosing that it is synthetic. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=potentially deceptive synthetic media#Correct. Authenticity matters when imagery implies lived experience or endorsement.
~ambiguous engagement signal#Not the best answer. Authenticity matters when imagery implies lived experience or endorsement.
~data minimisation failure#Not the best answer. Authenticity matters when imagery implies lived experience or endorsement.
~external validity and digital divide problem#Not the best answer. Authenticity matters when imagery implies lived experience or endorsement.
}

::HC-W8-M10::A health ministry uses an AI-generated image of a fictional patient without disclosing that it is synthetic. What is the strongest next response? {
=Disclose synthetic representation when viewers could reasonably infer a real testimonial or real event.#Correct. Authenticity matters when imagery implies lived experience or endorsement.
~Review comment content and other evidence before inferring attitudes from reaction counts.#Not the best answer. Authenticity matters when imagery implies lived experience or endorsement.
~Collect only the data needed for subscription and explain retention and use.#Not the best answer. Authenticity matters when imagery implies lived experience or endorsement.
~Assess reach and outcomes among rural, female, low-connectivity and disability groups before generalising.#Not the best answer. Authenticity matters when imagery implies lived experience or endorsement.
}

::HC-W8-M11::A post receives angry reactions, and the team concludes the audience rejected the health recommendation. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=ambiguous engagement signal#Correct. Platform reactions do not have a single stable meaning.
~data minimisation failure#Not the best answer. Platform reactions do not have a single stable meaning.
~external validity and digital divide problem#Not the best answer. Platform reactions do not have a single stable meaning.
~undisclosed sponsorship#Not the best answer. Platform reactions do not have a single stable meaning.
}

::HC-W8-M12::A post receives angry reactions, and the team concludes the audience rejected the health recommendation. What is the strongest next response? {
=Review comment content and other evidence before inferring attitudes from reaction counts.#Correct. Platform reactions do not have a single stable meaning.
~Collect only the data needed for subscription and explain retention and use.#Not the best answer. Platform reactions do not have a single stable meaning.
~Assess reach and outcomes among rural, female, low-connectivity and disability groups before generalising.#Not the best answer. Platform reactions do not have a single stable meaning.
~Require transparent disclosure of the paid relationship and maintain evidence standards for claims.#Not the best answer. Platform reactions do not have a single stable meaning.
}

::HC-W8-M13::A clinic collects birth dates, exact addresses and national IDs for a simple health newsletter signup. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=data minimisation failure#Correct. More data increases privacy risk without improving the communication function.
~external validity and digital divide problem#Not the best answer. More data increases privacy risk without improving the communication function.
~undisclosed sponsorship#Not the best answer. More data increases privacy risk without improving the communication function.
~content removal mistaken for outcome#Not the best answer. More data increases privacy risk without improving the communication function.
}

::HC-W8-M14::A clinic collects birth dates, exact addresses and national IDs for a simple health newsletter signup. What is the strongest next response? {
=Collect only the data needed for subscription and explain retention and use.#Correct. More data increases privacy risk without improving the communication function.
~Assess reach and outcomes among rural, female, low-connectivity and disability groups before generalising.#Not the best answer. More data increases privacy risk without improving the communication function.
~Require transparent disclosure of the paid relationship and maintain evidence standards for claims.#Not the best answer. More data increases privacy risk without improving the communication function.
~Monitor whether the claim persists, shifts channels or continues to influence beliefs and behaviour.#Not the best answer. More data increases privacy risk without improving the communication function.
}

::HC-W8-M15::A digital campaign performs well among urban men and is declared nationally effective. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=external validity and digital divide problem#Correct. Digital performance in one segment may not transport to the wider population.
~undisclosed sponsorship#Not the best answer. Digital performance in one segment may not transport to the wider population.
~content removal mistaken for outcome#Not the best answer. Digital performance in one segment may not transport to the wider population.
~confounding in digital observational analytics#Not the best answer. Digital performance in one segment may not transport to the wider population.
}

::HC-W8-M16::A digital campaign performs well among urban men and is declared nationally effective. What is the strongest next response? {
=Assess reach and outcomes among rural, female, low-connectivity and disability groups before generalising.#Correct. Digital performance in one segment may not transport to the wider population.
~Require transparent disclosure of the paid relationship and maintain evidence standards for claims.#Not the best answer. Digital performance in one segment may not transport to the wider population.
~Monitor whether the claim persists, shifts channels or continues to influence beliefs and behaviour.#Not the best answer. Digital performance in one segment may not transport to the wider population.
~Account for self-selection and use stronger comparison designs before making a causal claim.#Not the best answer. Digital performance in one segment may not transport to the wider population.
}
$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Health Communication/Week 08/Institutional
::HC-W8-I01::An influencer promotes a health product without disclosing payment from the programme. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=undisclosed sponsorship#Correct. Hidden sponsorship can mislead audiences about independence and credibility.
~content removal mistaken for outcome#Not the best answer. Hidden sponsorship can mislead audiences about independence and credibility.
~confounding in digital observational analytics#Not the best answer. Hidden sponsorship can mislead audiences about independence and credibility.
~engagement without comprehension#Not the best answer. Hidden sponsorship can mislead audiences about independence and credibility.
}

::HC-W8-I02::An influencer promotes a health product without disclosing payment from the programme. What is the strongest next response? {
=Require transparent disclosure of the paid relationship and maintain evidence standards for claims.#Correct. Hidden sponsorship can mislead audiences about independence and credibility.
~Monitor whether the claim persists, shifts channels or continues to influence beliefs and behaviour.#Not the best answer. Hidden sponsorship can mislead audiences about independence and credibility.
~Account for self-selection and use stronger comparison designs before making a causal claim.#Not the best answer. Hidden sponsorship can mislead audiences about independence and credibility.
~Measure comprehension and correct the ambiguity rather than treating views as success.#Not the best answer. Hidden sponsorship can mislead audiences about independence and credibility.
}

::HC-W8-I03::A platform removes a misleading post, and the programme declares the misinformation problem solved. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=content removal mistaken for outcome#Correct. Removal of one item does not measure information impact.
~confounding in digital observational analytics#Not the best answer. Removal of one item does not measure information impact.
~engagement without comprehension#Not the best answer. Removal of one item does not measure information impact.
~privacy risk in digital messaging#Not the best answer. Removal of one item does not measure information impact.
}

::HC-W8-I04::A platform removes a misleading post, and the programme declares the misinformation problem solved. What is the strongest next response? {
=Monitor whether the claim persists, shifts channels or continues to influence beliefs and behaviour.#Correct. Removal of one item does not measure information impact.
~Account for self-selection and use stronger comparison designs before making a causal claim.#Not the best answer. Removal of one item does not measure information impact.
~Measure comprehension and correct the ambiguity rather than treating views as success.#Not the best answer. Removal of one item does not measure information impact.
~Use consented, discreet reminder options and allow users to choose safe channels.#Not the best answer. Removal of one item does not measure information impact.
}

::HC-W8-I05::Users who click a diabetes ad later attend screening more often, and the team concludes the ad caused attendance. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=confounding in digital observational analytics#Correct. People predisposed to screening may be more likely to click and attend.
~engagement without comprehension#Not the best answer. People predisposed to screening may be more likely to click and attend.
~privacy risk in digital messaging#Not the best answer. People predisposed to screening may be more likely to click and attend.
~unsafe generative AI deployment#Not the best answer. People predisposed to screening may be more likely to click and attend.
}

::HC-W8-I06::Users who click a diabetes ad later attend screening more often, and the team concludes the ad caused attendance. What is the strongest next response? {
=Account for self-selection and use stronger comparison designs before making a causal claim.#Correct. People predisposed to screening may be more likely to click and attend.
~Measure comprehension and correct the ambiguity rather than treating views as success.#Not the best answer. People predisposed to screening may be more likely to click and attend.
~Use consented, discreet reminder options and allow users to choose safe channels.#Not the best answer. People predisposed to screening may be more likely to click and attend.
~Constrain knowledge sources, define prohibited advice, monitor outputs and escalate high-risk questions to humans.#Not the best answer. People predisposed to screening may be more likely to click and attend.
}

